hreat, risking free material loss. \n- **B: b4-f8** is safe but passive, reducing the bishop's influence.\n\nReason: Prioritizing the bishop's safety (B: b4-e7) preserves material equality and avoids falling into a tactical trap. The e7 square is defended by the king, immune to immediate threats, and keeps the bishop active for future play. Capturing the knight (dxe4) appears tempting but ultimately loses tempo and fails to capitalize on White's oversight due to the bishop's vulnerability.\n\nAnswer: B: b4-e7"}
